   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/Gram/ChangeOfFamily.lean",
   "fix": "Add `have hconj : (U.map (starRingEnd \ud835\udd5c)).det = starRingEnd \ud835\udd5c U.det := ((starRingEnd \ud835\udd5c).map_det U).symm`, then use `rw [gram_sum_smul, det_mul, det_mul, det_transpose, hconj]` and close with `simp [RCLike.conj_mul, mul_right_comm]` (or `ring_nf`/`grind`). In `det_gram_matrix_smul`, replace the `id` rewrite with `simp [det_gram_sum_smul, sq_abs]`.",
   "issue": "`det_gram_sum_smul` is a 9-lemma `rw` chain whose middle steps (`\u2190 RingHom.mapMatrix_apply, \u2190 RingHom.map_det`) prove `det (U.map conj) = conj (det U)` without stating it; renames or a coercion change would break the chain, and the reason the proof works is hidden. `det_gram_matrix_smul` (line 77) also rewrites with `RCLike.ofReal_real_eq_id, id`, which only works because that lemma is proved by `rfl`.",
   "line": 69
